From 0dd0c506c9833804628c6860384f547fd9aacee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:06:19 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/24] kcm_fonts: fonts first, text rendering section,
 previews only when asked

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Config keys, KConfigXT, D-Bus and behaviour unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- The six font rows now open the page (General, Fixed width, Small, Toolbar, Menu, Window title).
  "Adjust All Fonts..." moved below them into a "Change all:" row, next to a new "Adjust Global Scale..." button
  (link to Display, which owns scale; kcm_fonts/AdjustGlobalScale). The header warning action still exists.
- Untitled separator replaced by a section titled "Text rendering": Anti-aliasing ("Enable" -> "Smooth font edges"),
  exclude range (indented under it, disabled not hidden), Sub-pixel rendering, Hinting.
- Scale link uses KCMLauncher.openSystemSettings instead of open.
- Buddies for combos, accessible names for the two spin boxes.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_fonts.tsv (outer repo). 14 inventory rows kept.

Speed cause: PreviewImageProvider builds a PreviewRenderEngine(true) per image, whose constructor calls
FcInitReinitialize() (previewrenderengine.cpp), i.e. rescans all font directories, and the provider also writes
and re-reads the fontconfig file twice per image (previewimageprovider.cpp). The sub-pixel and hinting combo
delegates (9 images) requested these as soon as the page loaded, so on open the fontconfig rescan ran nine
times while the GUI thread needed fontconfig to lay out the six font rows. Fix: each combo requests its previews
only once its popup is first opened (aboutToShow), delegates have an empty source until then.
Not changed: the QtWidgets KFontChooserDialog still loads QFontDatabase on first click.
Numbers: before (0.5 CPU) in build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv; after: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-017, HIG-023, HIG-047, HIG-057, HIG-058, HIG-062.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
